\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120452 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119775 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74764043-e1e7-56d6-8f53-9d287a30e538" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Switching Two Rows"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9130b080-a9c6-517f-ab25-7cad6b7c57ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{28}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385450} {:answer/id #uuid "2cc8cf49-48b6-56f7-a5a1-3c2c3b03145d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385451} {:answer/id #uuid "5b4617a3-07c2-5172-a155-623760aaad73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385452} {:answer/id #uuid "0bfe9c29-4aa6-55d5-93bf-35a97039e836" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "Undefined" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385453} {:answer/id #uuid "0d8c6831-8791-54cd-90fc-843a91287a59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cc8cf49-48b6-56f7-a5a1-3c2c3b03145d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385451} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcf8fc37-a5d5-5e52-9ad0-52512dc41d1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a88ba8dd-cf2b-52e3-868f-43da972f2751" :question/math-academy-id "q-43076" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $det(A)=-28.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{5}↔{R}_{3}$ (switching the third and the fifth rows). What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "Since swapping any two rows changes the sign of the determinant to the opposite sign, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-det(A) \\\\  & =-(-28) \\\\  & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120453 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119776 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2f11b223-edd2-59b8-b761-164d56e29746" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Row by a Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "232073ae-c510-5f48-a5f3-9c541a6c13ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327238} {:answer/id #uuid "2dca7964-2f48-506b-9487-7a70e775af51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327343} {:answer/id #uuid "847167d8-21c4-560e-87d5-0b2c88f27b6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328078} {:answer/id #uuid "a753ec68-d63b-5cd4-9e4e-76d19214842b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-105" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328388} {:answer/id #uuid "f1616760-5bdf-56a2-b3ff-a0bf1de004f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "232073ae-c510-5f48-a5f3-9c541a6c13ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327238} :answer-field/id #uuid "07acf18c-dad7-5fe5-9a13-5d6b19b5cfb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329197}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d347b77d-0a2e-5499-b039-62abd2cb7bcf" :question/math-academy-id "q-43077" :question/problem "Suppose $A$ is a $6\\times 6$ matrix and $det(A)=35.$ The matrix $B$ is obtained from $A$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=-\\frac{3}{5}{R}_{1}.$ What is the value of $det(B)?$" :question/worked-solution "The row operation applied to $A$ consists of multiplying a row by the number $-\\frac{3}{5}.$\n\nWhen we do this, the determinant is multiplied by the same number. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-\\frac{3}{5}det(A) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}\\cdot 35 \\\\  & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329708 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119850 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e23ca5d-3f02-50d1-b1ef-ae61b56450f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327052} {:answer/id #uuid "14a5e586-4579-5e34-9e1c-dce342148ad6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327111} {:answer/id #uuid "4dbb949e-5f4c-59c7-bf5e-66b314182381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327608} {:answer/id #uuid "65393eb0-4103-5d97-99d7-da790317f3f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-216" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327815} {:answer/id #uuid "dce6b1a0-2064-56ac-85db-4f79d9ab1ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "108" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dbb949e-5f4c-59c7-bf5e-66b314182381" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327608} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b13a8ec-3480-5941-9bdf-880b590f86a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "47c11704-21a6-552f-bee3-3f4e3309d6d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-43081" :question/problem "Consider the matrices given below. Given that $A$ and $B$ are row equivalent matrices and $det(A)=-108$, find $det(B).$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $B$ can be obtained from $A$ by multiplying the $2$nd row by $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ \n\nSo, the determinant is multiplied by $-\\frac{1}{2}$ as well.\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot det(A) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-108) \\\\  & =54.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119851 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "272d9a54-ba97-5175-86df-0a78337da7b9" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant After Multiplying a Matrix by a Scalar"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8abf4f46-cb92-54d4-9c70-8a06f7b21b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119187} {:answer/id #uuid "b754331f-0621-514f-bb21-c33b15a5df9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119188} {:answer/id #uuid "d19fa999-5542-53c5-93ad-fb03f8d1b1df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119189} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b57cea-9992-